      "content": "This is where the line can become very blurry, as \"unaided memory\" is inherently vague. If the knowledge is a unique architecture or a highly specific non-standard structure, using it directly could be seen as incorporating their protected proprietary methods, not just general knowledge. It is safest to generalize the concept significantly before applying it elsewhere. If in doubt about the specificity, seek legal review to ensure you are only utilizing the abstract lessons learned, not their unique implementation details.",
